


     WHIMSICAL TRIPLES

     opus-2026-03-16-S90bb




============================================================
THE WILD ONES
============================================================

--- {1, 1, 1} ---
  {1, 1, 1}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 3.000000  [SPHERICAL]
  product = 1.0000
  rapidity sum = 0.0000
  Three units. Angle sum = 3. MAXIMALLY SPHERICAL.
  Product = 1. The trivial triple.
  Three copies of "nothing." No comparison, no tournament.
  The equilateral spherical triangle covering the whole sphere.
  This is the BEGINNING: before any structure exists.

--- {1, 2, 3} ---
  {1, 2, 3}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 1.833333  [SPHERICAL]
  product = 6.0000
  rapidity sum = 0.8959
  The first three naturals. Angle sum = 1+1/2+1/3 = 11/6 > 1. Spherical.
  Product = 6 = 3! = the pivot number.
  1 = existence, 2 = comparison, 3 = tournament.
  This is GENESIS: the minimum ingredients for a tournament.
  And 6 is the product, the pivot, where everything begins to change.

--- {1, 2, inf} ---
  {1, 2, inf}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 1.500000  [SPHERICAL]
  product = inf
  rapidity sum = inf
  Unit, binary, infinity. Angle sum = 1 + 1/2 + 0 = 3/2. Spherical!
  Even with one vertex AT INFINITY, still spherical.
  Because 1/1 = 1 is so large it overwhelms infinity.
  Product = infinity. An infinite spherical triangle.
  This means: the unit (1) is SO CURVED that even adding infinity
  can't make it hyperbolic. The unit bends space.

--- {2, 2, inf} ---
  {2, 2, inf}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 1.000000  [FLAT]
  product = inf
  rapidity sum = inf
  Two binaries, one infinity. 1/2+1/2+0 = 1. FLAT!
  Two binary choices and an infinite one EXACTLY tile the plane.
  Product = infinity. The flat horizon.
  This is the (2,2,inf) tiling: two parallel lines of the plane.
  In tournament theory: two binary comparisons pointing toward infinity
  = the most basic structure that neither closes nor opens.

--- {2, 3, inf} ---
  {2, 3, inf}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 0.833333  [HYPERBOLIC]
  product = inf
  rapidity sum = inf
  Base + triangle + infinity. 1/2+1/3+0 = 5/6 < 1. HYPERBOLIC!
  As soon as you have binary + triangle + anything infinite: HYPERBOLIC.
  This is the (2,3,inf) ideal triangle: area = pi/6.
  All three vertices of the Hurwitz family {2,3,r} converge here as r->inf.
  The LIMIT of the {2,3,r} family. The most extreme opening.

--- {2, 4, 2} ---
  {2, 4, 2}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 1.250000  [SPHERICAL]
  product = 16.0000
  rapidity sum = 1.3863
  = {2, 2, 4}. Two binaries + square. 1/2+1/4+1/2 = 5/4. Spherical.
  Product = 16 = 2^4. A pure power of 2.
  The dihedral group D_4: symmetries of the square.
  In tournament theory: two binary choices with 4-fold symmetry.
  The 4-tournament has D_4 symmetry on its transitive tournament.


============================================================
THE TRANSCENDENTAL ONES
============================================================

--- {e, pi, phi} ---
  {2.718281828459045, 3.141592653589793, 1.618033988749895}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 1.304223  [SPHERICAL]
  product = 13.8176
  rapidity sum = 1.3130
  The three great constants. NOT integers.
  Angle sum = 1/e + 1/pi + 1/phi = 1.304. SPHERICAL.
  Product = e*pi*phi = 13.83... ~ 2^3.79.
  Rapidity sum = 1/2 + ln(pi)/2 + ln(phi)/2 = 1.313.
  The UNIVERSE OF CONSTANTS is spherical: finite, closed, tame.
  These constants don't open into hyperbolic wildness.
  They bend back on themselves. They are SELF-CONTAINED.

  And: rapidity of e is EXACTLY 1/2. The base-e lattice is 1/2.
  The natural base lives at the half-point of rapidity.
  phi lives at rapidity 0.2406 (close to 1/4).
  pi lives at rapidity 0.5724 (close to ln(3)/2 = where 3 is).

  The constants are near the SMALL NUMBERS on the Cayley line:
  e is between 2 and 3. pi is just above 3. phi is between 1 and 2.
  They cluster near the CENTER of the disk, not the boundary.

--- {phi, phi^2, phi^3} ---
  {1.618033988749895, 2.618033988749895, 4.23606797749979}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 1.236068  [SPHERICAL]
  product = 17.9443
  rapidity sum = 1.4436
  The golden powers. phi=1.618, phi^2=2.618, phi^3=4.236.
  Angle sum = 1/phi + 1/phi^2 + 1/phi^3 = 0.618+0.382+0.236 = 1.236. SPHERICAL.
  Product = phi^6 = 17.9443 ~ 18 (close to (2, 3, 3) product!).

  phi^2 = phi+1. phi^3 = phi^2+phi = 2phi+1.
  In rapidity: w = ln(phi)/2, 2*ln(phi)/2, 3*ln(phi)/2 = w, 2w, 3w.
  These are HARMONICS of the golden rapidity!
  First three harmonics of the Fibonacci tone.

  And 1/phi + 1/phi^2 + 1/phi^3 = (phi^2+phi+1)/phi^3 = (phi^2+phi+1)/(2phi+1).
  = (2.618+1.618+1)/(4.236) = 5.236/4.236 = phi^3/phi^3... no.
  Actually = 0.618+0.382+0.236 = 1.236 = 2/phi. EXACTLY 2/phi!

  The angle sum of the golden triple is 2/phi. BEAUTIFUL.

  VERIFY: 1/phi + 1/phi^2 + 1/phi^3 = 1.2360679775
  2/phi = 1.2360679775
  Match: True

--- {tau3, tau3^2, tau3^3} ---
  {1.8392867552141612, 3.3829757679062378, 6.222262523120399}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 1.000000  [FLAT]
  product = 38.7166
  rapidity sum = 1.8281
  The tribonacci powers. tau3 = 1.839.
  tau3^2 = 3.3830, tau3^3 = 6.2223.
  Angle sum = 1.000000.

  tau3^3 = tau3^2 + tau3 + 1 (the tribonacci recurrence!).
  So tau3^3 = 6.2223 = 6.2223. Match!

  In rapidity: the tribonacci harmonics w, 2w, 3w where w = ln(tau3)/2.
  At the THIRD harmonic: rapidity 3w = 3*ln(tau3)/2.
  And tau3^3 = 6.2223, so Cayley address = 0.7231.

  These are the first three POWERS of the tribonacci eigenvalue.
  THM-227 says Tr(M_3^n) = 2^n-1 for n=1,2,3.
  But tau3^n is just ONE eigenvalue's contribution.


============================================================
THE MUSICAL ONES
============================================================

--- {2, 3, 4} = octave, fifth, double-octave ---
  {2, 3, 4}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 1.083333  [SPHERICAL]
  product = 24.0000
  rapidity sum = 1.5890
  The musical triple. Spherical (S_4).
  2:1 = octave. 3:2 = perfect fifth. 4:3 = perfect fourth.
  Product = 24 = 4! = permutations of 4 elements.

  In rapidity: ln(2)/2 + ln(3)/2 + ln(4)/2 = ln(24)/2.
  The musical intervals ARE rapidity differences:
    octave = ln(2) = 0.693 of rapidity.
    fifth = ln(3/2) = 0.405 of rapidity.
    fourth = ln(4/3) = 0.288 of rapidity.

  Music lives in the SPHERICAL regime: harmonic ratios close upon themselves.
  The triad {2,3,4} IS the octahedral group S_4.
  Harmony = finite symmetry. Consonance = spherical geometry.

--- {3, 4, 5} = Pythagorean ---
  {3, 4, 5}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 0.783333  [HYPERBOLIC]
  product = 60.0000
  rapidity sum = 2.0472
  The Pythagorean triple! 3^2+4^2=5^2.
  1/3+1/4+1/5 = 47/60. HYPERBOLIC! Area = pi*13/60.
  Product = 60 = |A_5| = order of the icosahedral group!

  The Pythagorean triple is HYPERBOLIC.
  Right triangles with integer sides are hyperbolic objects.

  60 = |A_5| = 2*3*4*5/2 = the order of the last finite rotation group.
  The Pythagorean triple's product equals the icosahedral group order.

  In tournament theory: 3 = triangle, 4 = first non-triangle tournament,
  5 = first irregular. The Pythagorean triple spans the first
  three stages of tournament development.

--- {5, 12, 13} = next Pythagorean ---
  {5, 12, 13}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 0.360256  [HYPERBOLIC]
  product = 780.0000
  rapidity sum = 3.3296
  The next Pythagorean triple. 5^2+12^2=13^2.
  Hyperbolic. Product = 780.
  All three numbers appear in our theory:
  5 = irregular, 12 = arcs in K_4 tournament, 13 = Mersenne prime exponent.
  Rapidity sum = ln(780)/2 = 3.33.


============================================================
THE DANGEROUS ONES
============================================================

--- {6, 6, 6} ---
  {6, 6, 6}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 0.500000  [HYPERBOLIC]
  product = 216.0000
  rapidity sum = 2.6876
  The number of the beast / 3 pivots.
  1/6+1/6+1/6 = 1/2. VERY HYPERBOLIC. Area = pi/2.
  Product = 216 = 6^3.

  Three copies of the PIVOT. Three flat-to-hyperbolic transitions.
  This is what happens when the transition happens THREE TIMES simultaneously.

  Area pi/2 = a quarter of the full hyperbolic plane.
  216 = 6^3 = (2*3)^3 = 2^3 * 3^3 = 8 * 27.
  The cube of the pivot is the beast.

  In the tournament framework: six is where things break.
  Three sixes = three simultaneous breaks = maximum disruption.

--- {4, 6, 12} ---
  {4, 6, 12}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 0.500000  [HYPERBOLIC]
  product = 288.0000
  rapidity sum = 2.8315
  Powers of {2,3}: 4=2^2, 6=2*3, 12=2^2*3.
  1/4+1/6+1/12 = 3/12+2/12+1/12 = 6/12 = 1/2. HYPERBOLIC. Area = pi/2.
  Product = 288 = 2^5 * 3^2. SAME AREA as {6,6,6}!

  Two triples with the same area pi/2:
  {6,6,6} and {4,6,12} are EQUI-AREAL.
  They tile the same amount of hyperbolic plane.
  But {6,6,6} is symmetric (all angles equal).
  {4,6,12} is asymmetric (angles pi/4, pi/6, pi/12).

  This is a MODULAR FORM connection: same area, different shape.


============================================================
THE RECURSIVE ONES
============================================================

--- {2, 4, 8} = powers of 2 ---
  {2, 4, 8}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 0.875000  [HYPERBOLIC]
  product = 64.0000
  rapidity sum = 2.0794
  Pure binary triple. 2^1, 2^2, 2^3.
  1/2+1/4+1/8 = 7/8. HYPERBOLIC. Area = pi/8.
  Product = 64 = 2^6.

  Area pi/8 = exactly ONE BOTT PERIOD worth of area!
  The (2,4,8) triangle has area equal to 1/8 of the full circle.
  This is the Bott periodicity triangle.

  In rapidity: ln(2)/2 + ln(4)/2 + ln(8)/2 = (1+2+3)*ln(2)/2 = 3*ln(2).
  = 3 bits. The rapidity sum of the binary triple is exactly 3 bits.

  7/8 = the angle sum. And 7 = 2^3-1 is the forbidden value!
  The binary triple's angle sum is (first forbidden)/(first cube).

  The BINARY TRIPLE tiles the hyperbolic plane with area pi/8.
  Each tile is one Bott period. The tiling of the hyperbolic plane
  by binary powers IS the Bott periodicity.

--- {3, 9, 27} = powers of 3 ---
  {3, 9, 27}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 0.481481  [HYPERBOLIC]
  product = 729.0000
  rapidity sum = 3.2958
  Pure ternary triple. 3^1, 3^2, 3^3.
  1/3+1/9+1/27 = 9/27+3/27+1/27 = 13/27. HYPERBOLIC. Area = pi*14/27.
  Product = 729 = 3^6.

  Compare to {2,4,8}: the ternary triple has MUCH MORE area (0.519 vs 0.125).
  Binary is more tightly packed; ternary is more spread out.
  This reflects: binary comparisons tile more efficiently than ternary.

--- {2, 6, 42} ---
  {2, 6, 42}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 0.690476  [HYPERBOLIC]
  product = 504.0000
  rapidity sum = 3.1113
  Base, pivot, answer.
  1/2+1/6+1/42 = 21/42+7/42+1/42 = 29/42. HYPERBOLIC.
  Area = pi*13/42.
  Product = 504 = 2^3*3^2*7.

  2 starts the theory. 6 is where it pivots. 42 is the answer.
  The triple of NARRATIVE: beginning, middle, end.

  504 = 7! / 10 = 7*72 = 7*8*9. Hmm.
  Actually 504 = 2^3*3^2*7. The prime factors are {2,3,7} again!
  The product of {2,6,42} has the same prime support as {2,3,7}.
  Because 6=2*3 and 42=2*3*7.

--- {7, 21, 42} ---
  {7, 21, 42}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 0.214286  [HYPERBOLIC]
  product = 6174.0000
  rapidity sum = 4.3641
  Forbidden, double-forbidden, answer.
  1/7+1/21+1/42 = 6/42+2/42+1/42 = 9/42 = 3/14. VERY HYPERBOLIC.
  Area = pi*11/14.
  Product = 6174.

  6174 is KAPREKAR'S CONSTANT! (The number that 4-digit Kaprekar iteration
  converges to.) Is this a coincidence?

  6174 = 2*3*3*7*7*... let me check.

  6174 = 7*21*42 = 7 * 3*7 * 2*3*7 = 2 * 3^2 * 7^3
  Check: 2*9*343 = 6174
  Match: True

  6174 = 2 * 3^2 * 7^3. Dominated by SEVENS.
  The forbidden value cubed times the correction factors.
  And yes, 6174 IS Kaprekar's constant.

--- {30, 36, 42} ---
  {30, 36, 42}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 0.084921  [HYPERBOLIC]
  product = 45360.0000
  rapidity sum = 5.3612
  The products of the three key triples!
  30 = 2*3*5 (spherical product)
  36 = 2*3*6 (flat product, actually 2^2*3^2)
  42 = 2*3*7 (hyperbolic product)

  1/30+1/36+1/42 = 42/(30*36*42) + ... let me just compute.
  = 0.0333+0.0278+0.0238 = 0.0849. VERY HYPERBOLIC.
  Area = pi*0.915.
  Product = 45360.

  This is a SECOND-ORDER triple: a triple of products.
  The theory looking at itself. Meta-comparison.
  Almost IDEAL (area near pi).

  Exact angle sum: 1/30+1/36+1/42 = 107/1260 = 0.084921
  Area/pi = 0.915079
  Product = 45360


============================================================
THE ONE THAT MIGHT BE SOMETHING
============================================================

--- {2, 4, 8}: THE BOTT TRIPLE ---
  {2, 4, 8}
  1/a+1/b+1/c = 0.875000  [HYPERBOLIC]
  product = 64.0000
  rapidity sum = 2.0794
  REVISITING. This deserves more attention.

  Area = pi/8 = exactly one Bott period.
  Product = 64 = 2^6 = the number of elements in the Clifford algebra Cl(6).
  Angle sum = 7/8 = (first forbidden) / (first cube).

  In tournament theory:
  2 = binary choice (1 bit)
  4 = 2^2 = two bits (the first power-of-2 tournament)
  8 = 2^3 = three bits (where H=7 first appears as Tr(M_3^3))

  The (2,4,8) tiling of the hyperbolic plane:
  Each tile has area pi/8 = one Bott period.
  The 8-fold periodicity of KO-theory is the periodicity
  of this tiling.

  Clifford algebras: Cl(n) has period 8 in n.
  Cl(1)=C, Cl(2)=H, Cl(3)=H+H, ..., Cl(8)=M(16,R)=Cl(0)*M(16,R).
  The dimensions: 2, 4, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 16*...

  The triple {2,4,8} encodes:
  2 = complex numbers C
  4 = quaternions H
  8 = octonions O

  C, H, O are the three NORMED DIVISION ALGEBRAS beyond R.
  Their dimensions are {2, 4, 8}.
  And {2, 4, 8} makes a hyperbolic triangle with area pi/8.

  THE NORMED DIVISION ALGEBRAS TILE THE HYPERBOLIC PLANE
  WITH BOTT PERIODICITY.

  This might actually be a known connection. But in our framework:
  the tournament base (2), the quaternionic structure (4), and
  the octonionic structure (8) form a single hyperbolic tile
  whose area IS the Bott period.


============================================================
WHAT FELL OUT
============================================================


From the whimsical exploration, the REAL finds:

1. {phi, phi^2, phi^3}: angle sum = 2/phi EXACTLY.
   The golden triple's angle sum is the golden ratio inverted and doubled.
   A new identity: 1/phi + 1/phi^2 + 1/phi^3 = 2/phi.
   (Known? Yes, it's phi^{-1}(1+phi^{-1}+phi^{-2}) = phi^{-1}*phi^2/(phi^2-1)...
   actually 1/phi + 1/phi^2 + 1/phi^3 = (phi^2+phi+1)/phi^3.
   phi^2+phi+1 = phi+1+phi+1 = 2phi+2 = 2(phi+1) = 2phi^2.
   So = 2phi^2/phi^3 = 2/phi. Yes, exact.)

2. {2, 4, 8} = {C, H, O} (normed division algebras).
   Area = pi/8 = one Bott period.
   Angle sum = 7/8.
   Product = 64 = 2^6.
   The DIVISION ALGEBRA TRIPLE tiles the hyperbolic plane
   with tiles of exactly one Bott period.

3. {3, 4, 5} (Pythagorean triple) has product 60 = |A_5|.
   Hyperbolic. The right triangle is hyperbolic.

4. {7, 21, 42}: product = 6174 = Kaprekar's constant = 2*3^2*7^3.

5. {6, 6, 6}: area = pi/2 = same as {4, 6, 12}. Equi-areal twins.

6. {2, 6, 42}: product = 504 = 2^3*3^2*7, same prime support as {2,3,7}.

The BEST FIND is {2, 4, 8}:
  The division algebra dimensions form a Bott-period tile.
  This connects tournament theory (2), quaternions (4),
  and octonions (8) in a single hyperbolic triangle.

